{
    "id": "PikaH3FlexT2VA",
    "description": "Text to video with audio through Pika H3 Flex, Pika's adapter over MiniMax-H3. The 't2va' workflow runs with no keyframe, so the clip is generated on the chosen 16:9 canvas from the prompt alone; it runs on the keyframe partition ('transformer') with Pika's fl2va adapter, as Pika's own release does. Pika H3 Flex is an adapter over MiniMax-H3's own weights: the five weight components (transformer, transformer_ref, text_encoder, vae, audio_vae) are loaded from MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3, pinned at the commit the H3 templates load (0919fb68, the same tensors as the 42ed227e base Pika's adapter manifest names, sampled), so they share H3's int8 cache; only the scheduler, tokenizer and processor come from Pika's repo. The adapter's sampler is fixed: its blocks run the 7-point denoising_step_list [1000, 750, 500, 250, 100, 40, 0] (6 transformer passes) on their own shift, so the template sets no num_inference_steps and no scheduler shift - stated in configuration.configs only so validate counts the passes. Seeds are not comparable with the H3 templates: the same seed on the same prompt gives a different clip, so an A/B against H3 compares samples, not a matched pair. The base match itself is sampled (Pika's own runs against the pinned base, not a bit-exact reproduction). 'resolution' picks a 16:9 bucket - 480p is 832x480, 768p is 1344x768; other ratios of the same tiers (multiples of 32): 9:16 480x832 / 768x1344, 1:1 480x480 / 768x768, 4:3 640x480 / 1024x768, 3:4 480x640 / 768x1024, 21:9 960x416 / 1536x672 - pass width and height for one. The weights load at int8 SDNQ (host_ram_gb 69).",
    "summary": "Pika H3 Flex text to video with audio: MiniMax-H3 under Pika's 6-pass adapter.",
    "cost": [
        {
            "device": "cuda",
            "name": "RTX 3090",
            "vram_gb": 24,
            "minutes": 2.25
        }
    ],
    "cost_drivers": [
        "num_frames",
        "width",
        "height",
        "weights_dtype",
        "attention_backend",
        "cache"
    ],
    "vram_estimate": {
        "base_gb": 16.3,
        "bytes_per_voxel": 28.71,
        "bytes_per_guide_voxel": 28.71,
        "voxel_variables": [
            "width",
            "height",
            "num_frames"
        ],
        "reason": "VAE decode's conv3d activation scales with the voxel count width * height * num_frames; base_gb and bytes_per_voxel are calibrated from two real runs: image-to-video's family baseline at 960x544x124 (on-demand VAE) succeeded at 18.03 GiB peak reserved (docs/WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md), and video-with-audio-768p at 1344x768x345 (the family's own num_frames ceiling) OOM'd mid-denoise needing >=25.82 GiB - 20.25 GiB already allocated plus a refused 5.57 GiB allocation, on a 23.56 GiB card (job 282172105da1, 2026-09-22) - closing the gap #265/#266 left the H3 family with nothing declared to check the engine's vram_estimate machinery against (#324)"
    },
    "host_ram_gb": 69,
    "variables": {
        "prompt": "A weathered lighthouse keeper climbs the spiral stairs at dusk with a brass lantern, wind rattling the windows. SHOT 1 (0-3s): low angle on the iron stairs as his boots ring on each step. SHOT 2 (3-5s): hard cut, the lamp room: he sets the lantern down and looks out at a storm rolling in over a grey sea. SOUND: wind howling around the tower, boots on iron, distant surf, a low cello drone. Nobody speaks. No subtitles, no captions, no text.",
        "num_frames": 124,
        "resolution": "480p",
        "width": 832,
        "height": 480,
        "weights_dtype": "{int8}",
        "seed": null,
        "attention_backend": "sparse",
        "sparse_tau": 0.5,
        "sparse_topk": 0.15,
        "cache": null
    },
    "variable_constraints": {
        "num_frames": {
            "modulus": 17,
            "remainder": 5,
            "min_frames": 124,
            "max_frames": 345,
            "snap": "up",
            "reason": "the video VAE encodes 17 * n + 5 frames, and Pika H3 Flex generates between 5 and 15 seconds at 24 fps (120..360 frames, snapped up onto the 17 * n + 5 grid)"
        },
        "width": {
            "modulus": 32,
            "remainder": 0,
            "reason": "Pika H3 Flex's canvas is a multiple of 32 on both axes, and MiniMax-H3's pipeline refuses one that is not only after the weights have loaded; refused here instead, with no 'snap', since rounding would be a silent change to the size asked for"
        },
        "height": {
            "modulus": 32,
            "remainder": 0,
            "reason": "Pika H3 Flex's canvas is a multiple of 32 on both axes, and MiniMax-H3's pipeline refuses one that is not only after the weights have loaded; refused here instead, with no 'snap', since rounding would be a silent change to the size asked for"
        }
    },
    "presets": {
        "resolution": {
            "480p": {
                "width": 832,
                "height": 480
            },
            "768p": {
                "width": 1344,
                "height": 768
            }
        }
    },
    "seed": "variable:seed",
    "steps": [
